{%- comment -%}
  guide-download — the "your guide is ready" delivery page. 6 uses, all on the
  `guide-download` page suffix:
    engagement-ring-guide-download          eternity-ring-guide-download
    plain-wedding-ring-guide-download       diamond-and-gemstone-guide-download
    diamond-gemstone-wedding-ring-guide-download
    ring-and-jewellery-care-guide-download

  PORTED FROM LIVE'S `guide-download`. Setting IDs kept: logo · show_logo ·
  heading · body · back_link · back_label · fallback_link.

  ONE TEMPLATE, SIX PAGES — so nothing page-specific can live in section
  settings. Everything that differs comes from the page's own `guide`
  metafields, which already exist in the store:

    guide.pdf_url          url            the PDF itself
    guide.cover_image      file_reference front cover
    guide.button_label     text           defaults to "Download the guide"
    guide.analytics_name   text           defaults to the page title
    guide.delay_ms         integer        auto-download delay, defaults 1200

  A guide with no `pdf_url` says so rather than showing a dead button. That is
  deliberate: the pages exist before some of the PDFs do.

  CHANGED FOR v3: the inline <script> and <style> are gone. Behaviour moved to
  assets/fye-ui.js and is driven by the data attributes on the wrapper below —
  the theme has one place for JS, and a script tag in a section runs before the
  rest of the page has streamed. Styling is in {% stylesheet %} on tokens.

  THE AUTO-DOWNLOAD IS LIVE'S BEHAVIOUR, KEPT: after the delay the browser is
  sent to the PDF, once per session per guide. It is aggressive, but someone
  arriving here has just asked for the file, and the button remains for anyone
  who lands back on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign g = page.metafields.guide
  assign pdf = g.pdf_url.value
  assign cover = g.cover_image.value
  assign btn_label = g.button_label.value | default: 'Download the guide'
  assign delay = g.delay_ms.value | default: 1200
  assign track_name = g.analytics_name.value | default: page.title

  comment
    Built here, not chained inside the image_tag argument: `alt: page.title |
    append: '...'` applies the append to the OUTPUT of image_tag (conventions
    §5), which printed a stray "front cover" as visible text under the cover
    on every thank-you page while leaving the alt itself empty.
  endcomment
  assign cover_alt = page.title | append: ', front cover'
-%}

<section class="gdl band band--ivory" data-screen-label="Guide download"
         {%- if pdf != blank %} data-fye-guide-dl
         data-pdf="{{ pdf | escape }}"
         data-name="{{ track_name | escape }}"
         data-delay="{{ delay }}"{% endif -%}>
  <div class="wrap gdl__in">

    {%- if s.show_logo and s.logo != blank -%}
      {{ s.logo | image_url: width: 320 | image_tag:
         loading: 'eager',
         widths: '160, 320',
         sizes: '160px',
         class: 'gdl__logo',
         alt: shop.name }}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if cover != blank -%}
      {{ cover | image_url: width: 640 | image_tag:
         loading: 'eager',
         widths: '320, 640',
         sizes: '(max-width: 560px) 60vw, 300px',
         class: 'gdl__cover',
         alt: cover_alt }}
    {%- endif -%}

    <h1 class="gdl__title">{{ s.heading | default: page.title }}</h1>

    <div class="lead gdl__copy">
      {{- s.body | default: '<p>Your download should begin automatically in a moment. If it does not, use the button below.</p>' -}}
    </div>

    {%- if pdf != blank -%}
      <a class="btn" href="{{ pdf }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-fye-guide-btn>
        {{- btn_label -}}
      </a>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="gdl__soon">
        This guide is coming very soon.
        {%- if s.fallback_link != blank %} <a href="{{ s.fallback_link }}">Browse our other guides</a>.{% endif -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if page.content != blank -%}
      <div class="prose gdl__intro">{{ page.content }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.back_link != blank -%}
      <p class="gdl__back">
        <a href="{{ s.back_link }}">{{ s.back_label | default: 'Back to the guides' }}</a>
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .gdl__in { max-width: 640px; margin-inline: auto; text-align: center; }
.fye .gdl__logo { display: block; margin: 0 auto var(--s7); width: 160px; height: auto; }
/* The one shadow in the theme, and it earns it: the cover is a photograph of
   a physical object and reads as paper lifted off the band. */
.fye .gdl__cover {
  display: block;
  margin: 0 auto var(--s6);
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 300px;
  height: auto;
  box-shadow: 0 12px 34px rgba(35, 61, 71, 0.16);
}
.fye .gdl__title { margin: 0 0 var(--s4); }
.fye .gdl__copy { margin: 0 auto var(--s6); max-width: 30em; }
.fye .gdl__copy :where(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fye .gdl__soon { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .gdl__intro { margin: var(--s9) auto 0; max-width: 34em; text-align: left; }
.fye .gdl__back { margin: var(--s6) 0 0; font-size: var(--fs-small); }
.fye .gdl__back a { border-bottom: var(--hairline); }

@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .gdl__cover { max-width: 210px; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Guide download",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "logo", "label": "Logo" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_logo", "label": "Show the logo", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "info": "Defaults to the page title." },
    {
      "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Confirmation copy",
      "default": "<p>Your download should begin automatically in a moment. If it does not, use the button below.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "url", "id": "back_link", "label": "Back link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "back_label", "label": "Back link text", "default": "Back to the guides" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "fallback_link", "label": "Fallback link", "info": "Shown when a guide has no PDF yet." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Guide download" }]
}
{% endschema %}
